\par ```markdown\line # Skill: References Quality \\& Format\line \line ## When This Skill Applies\line Every generated monograph during reference compilation phase.\line \line ## The Problem It Solves\line 
Clinical references come from various sources (PubMed, FDA labels, EMA documents) \line with inconsistent formatting. We need:\line - Consistent format per SOP standards\line - Prioritization of high-quality sources (peer-reviewed > case reports)\line 
- Validation that citations match claims in text\line \line ## Rules\line \line ### Rule 1: Reference Prioritization\line When selecting references for a section, prioritize:\line 1. Randomized controlled trials (RCTs) - Weight: 1.0\line 
2. Systematic reviews/meta-analyses - Weight: 0.95\line 3. Cohort studies - Weight: 0.8\line 4. Case-control studies - Weight: 0.7\line 5. Case reports - Weight: 0.3\line 6. Expert consensus - Weight: 0.1\line \line ### Rule 2: Publication Date Filtering
\line - For pharmacology sections: Include all relevant historical context (no date limit)\line - For clinical efficacy: Prioritize last 10 years (50% of references), allow older foundational studies\line 
- For safety: Prioritize last 5 years; include all major safety alerts regardless of date\line \line ### Rule 3: Source Validation\line Before citing a source, verify:\line - \\
[ ] Is it from an authoritative database? (PubMed, FDA, EMA, peer-reviewed journal)\line - \\[ ] Is author/journal name realistic? (catch AI-generated fake citations)\line - \\[ ] Does abstract/full text actually support the claim being made?\line \line 
### Rule 4: Reference Formatting (SOP Standard)\line Example format:\line "Author AA, Author BB. Article Title. Journal Name. 2023;45(3):234-245. doi: 10.xxxx/xxxxx."\line \line ## Quality Metrics (How to Measure Success)\line }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16077218\charrsid16077218 \u10003\'3f}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16077218\charrsid16077218  Zero formatting inconsistencies in reference list\line \u10003\'3f \u8805\'3d
70% of citations are level 1-2 evidence (RCT/SR) per section\line \u10003\'3f Each claim in text has at least one supporting citation\line \u10003\'3f Average publication year of references reflects recency goals per section\line \line ## Fe
edback Triggers (When to Update This Skill)\line IF: Reviewers flag "missing critical reference"\line THEN: Review selection rules, may need to lower prioritization threshold\line \line IF: "Outdated information" feedback increases\line 
THEN: Tighten publication year filters\line \line ## Version\line v1.2 | Updated: 2024-01-10 | Author: Medical Director\line ```
\par 7.2 Skill Learning Flow
\par ```\line Stage 1: CREATION \\& UPLOAD\line   Medical Director writes skill file (NL document)\line   \u8594\'3f Uploads via web interface\line   \u8594\'3f System parses rules using NLP\line   \u8594\'3f Stores in skill file database (version 1)\line 
\line Stage 2: APPLICATION\line   When generating monograph:\line   \u8594\'3f For each relevant section, load applicable skill files\line   \u8594\'3f Inject skill rules into Claude prompt\line   \u8594\'3f
 Claude generates output respecting skill constraints\line   \u8594\'3f Output validated against skill metrics\line   \u8594\'3f Log: Which skills applied, did they improve quality?\line \line Stage 3: FEEDBACK COLLECTION\line 
  After HCP reviews monograph:\line   \u8594\'3f HCP provides feedback (rating, comments)\line   \u8594\'3f System analyzes feedback for skill-related issues\line   \u8594\'3f Examples:\line      "Pharmacology section too technical" \line      \u8594\'3f
 Suggests updating Pharmacology skill file\line      \line      "Missing important safety information"\line      \u8594\'3f Suggests updating Safety skill file (why wasn't it found?)\line \line Stage 4: LEARNING \\& REFINEMENT\line 
  System provides recommendations to Medical Director:\line   "Skill 'Pharmacology Quality Checks' was applied to 15 monographs.\line    Feedback analysis shows 3 users complained about 'technical jargon.'\line    Recommendation: Add rule
 about readability level.\line    Suggested revision: \\[auto-generated diff]"\line   \line   Medical Director can:\line   \u8594\'3f Accept suggested revision (\u8594\'3f v1.3)\line   \u8594\'3f Modify revision manually (\u8594\'3f v1.3)\line   \u8594
\'3f Reject and keep current version (\u8594\'3f no change)\line \line Stage 5: A/B TESTING (Future)\line   Test old skill file (v1.2) vs. new skill file (v1.3):\line   \u8594\'3f Generate same monograph with both versions\line   \u8594\'3f
 Get feedback from independent reviewers\line   \u8594\'3f Measure which version produces better quality\line   \u8594\'3f If v1.3 wins, roll out to all future generations\line ```
